{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5357) to implement the `groups` utility at `cmd/groups/main.go`. The task title is \"[stitch] srd043-groups R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1 (implementation)\". The specific requirements are:\n   - R1 (srd043 R1.1): No arguments → print group memberships of current user to stdout\n   - R2 (srd043 R1.2): With username arguments → print group memberships for each specified user\n   - R3 (srd043 R1.3): Exit 0 on success, non-zero if any specified user doesn't exist\n   - R4 (srd043 R2.1): Support --help flag printing usage to stdout, exit 0\n   \n   Design decisions require calling `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at main start and writing output to os.Stdout / errors to os.Stderr.\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (compiles), AC2 (no-arg prints current user groups), AC3 (named user works), AC4 (--help works), AC5 (go vet clean).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `groups` coreutils utility\n   - Differential testing pattern against Homebrew `ggroups` reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `os/user` package for user and group lookups\n   - Output format: no prefix for no-arg mode, \"user : group1 group2\" for named-user mode\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n   - No git commands allowed (managed externally by orchestrator)\n   - Build with `go build -o bin/groups ./cmd/groups/`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd043-groups.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for the groups utility\n     - R1: Default behavior (R1.1 no-args current user, R1.2 named users, R1.3 error handling)\n     - R2: Output format (R2.1 no prefix for no-args, R2.2 \"user : groups\" format for named users, R2.3 system database order)\n     - R3: Differential testing requirements (not in scope for this task)\n     - Non-goals: no flags beyond --help/--version, no GIDs, no stdin\n   \n   - `cmd/groups/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - The main deliverable file\n     - Must implement groups utility matching GNU ggroups behavior\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (existing, provided in context)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` that must be called at start of main\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n   \n   - Existing cmd/ utilities in context provide patterns (whoami already exists and is implemented per code_status)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call was made (reading the SRD) before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full specification for groups\n   - Was about to plan and implement the utility when the summary request interrupted\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt containing all project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, task requirements, constraints, description with required reading/files/requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/groups/main.go` implementing the groups utility with:\n     - Copyright header\n     - SIGPIPE handler installation\n     - No-arg mode: print current user's groups (space-separated, no prefix)\n     - Named-user mode: print \"user : group1 group2 ...\" for each user\n     - Error handling: stderr message for nonexistent users, exit 1 if any failed\n     - --help flag support\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/groups ./cmd/groups/`\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/groups/...`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd043-groups.yaml`) and was about to plan and implement `cmd/groups/main.go`. The SRD confirmed the requirements:\n   - R1.1: No args → space-separated group names, single line, newline, exit 0\n   - R1.2: With USER args → one line per user, exit 0\n   - R1.3: Nonexistent user → error to stderr, continue processing, exit 1 if any not found\n   - R2.1: No args → no prefix output\n   - R2.2: Named user → \"user : group1 group2 ...\" format\n   - R2.3: Group names in system database order\n   - Non-goals: no flags beyond --help/--version, no GIDs, no stdin\n   \n   No code has been written yet. The implementation needs to use Go's `os/user` package for `user.Lookup()`, `user.Current()`, and group ID lookups.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Create `cmd/groups/main.go` with the full implementation. The approach should be:\n   1. Write the complete file with copyright header, package declaration, imports\n   2. `main()` calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`, checks for --help, then dispatches to no-arg or named-user mode\n   3. No-arg: `user.Current()` → get group IDs → resolve to names → print space-separated\n   4. Named-user: for each arg, `user.Lookup()` → get group IDs → resolve to names → print \"user : groups\"\n   5. Error case: if lookup fails, print error to stderr, set exit code to 1, continue\n   6. Then verify with `go build -o bin/groups ./cmd/groups/` and `go vet ./cmd/groups/...`\n   \n   This directly corresponds to the task description which says: \"Follow these steps in order... 3. **Implement** — Complete the work described in Requirements and Files to Create/Modify.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5357/51d72f61-5a21-4a96-84ea-8e7312cecd07.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51d72f61-5a21-4a96-84ea-8e7312cecd07","uuid":"574eafb1-91e5-4f2d-802d-ae2d4ac32a1b","timestamp":"2026-05-20T13:43:59.853Z","isSynthetic":true}
