{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VVz8Tku9BA8vYnfNMmH3m1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found all the files you requested. Here's the complete content for your implementation reference:\n\n## 1. cmd/whoami/main.go\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Implements srd042-whoami R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/user\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nconst helpText = `Usage: whoami [OPTION]...\nPrint the user name associated with the current effective user ID.\nSame as id -un.\n\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n\nconst versionText = `whoami (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\targs := os.Args[1:]\n\targs = parseFlags(args)\n\n\tif len(args) > 0 {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'whoami --help' for more information.\")\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tu, err := user.Current()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: cannot find name for user ID %d: %v\\n\", os.Geteuid(), err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tif _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, u.Username); err != nil {\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n\tfor len(args) > 0 {\n\t\tswitch args[0] {\n\t\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\tcase \"--\":\n\t\t\treturn args[1:]\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\") && len(args[0]) > 1 {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'whoami --help' for more information.\")\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn args\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn args\n}\n```\n\n## 2. cmd/logname/main.go (user lookup utility)\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Implements srd053-logname R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.3.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nconst helpText = `Usage: logname [OPTION]\nPrint the name of the current user.\n\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n\nconst versionText = `logname (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\targs := os.Args[1:]\n\targs = parseFlags(args)\n\n\tif len(args) > 0 {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"logname: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'logname --help' for more information.\")\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tloginName := os.Getenv(\"LOGNAME\")\n\tif loginName == \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"logname: no login name\")\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tif _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, loginName); err != nil {\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n\tfor len(args) > 0 {\n\t\tswitch args[0] {\n\t\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\tcase \"--\":\n\t\t\treturn args[1:]\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\") && len(args[0]) > 1 {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"logname: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'logname --help' for more information.\")\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn args\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn args\n}\n```\n\n## 3. pkg/sys/sigpipe.go\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage sys\n\nimport (\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/signal\"\n\t\"syscall\"\n)\n\n// InstallSIGPIPEHandler installs a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to\n// exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching\n// GNU coreutils behavior.\n// R1.5: uses signal.Notify with a buffered channel; does not use signal.Ignore.\n// R1.6: safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine.\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n\tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n\tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n\tgo func() {\n\t\t<-c\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t}()\n}\n```\n\n## Key Patterns to Note\n\n1. **SIGPIPE Handler**: Both `whoami` and `logname` call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at the start of `main()`. This uses Go's `signal.Notify()` with a buffered channel and a goroutine to handle pipe closures gracefully.\n\n2. **Flag Parsing**: Both utilities use a simple manual flag parsing approach with a `parseFlags()` function that:\n   - Handles `--help` and `--version` flags\n   - Uses `--` to terminate flag processing\n   - Validates unrecognized flags starting with `-`\n   - Returns remaining args for operand processing\n\n3. **User Lookup Methods**:\n   - `whoami`: Uses `os/user.Current()` to get the effective user\n   - `logname`: Uses `os.Getenv(\"LOGNAME\")` to get the login name\n\n4. **Error Handling**: Both utilities use `os.Exit()` with appropriate error codes and write error messages to stderr.\n\n5. **Output Handling**: Both use `fmt.Fprintln()` and check for write errors with proper exit codes."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51d72f61-5a21-4a96-84ea-8e7312cecd07","uuid":"1648a1af-6e36-4d3c-88fb-ae1740239bfe","timestamp":"2026-05-20T13:44:28.634Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the patterns used in this Go coreutils project. Please find and show me:\n\n1. The content of `cmd/whoami/main.go` (a simple utility that should be a good pattern reference)\n2. Any other simple cmd/ utility that does user lookups or group lookups\n3. The content of `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` to confirm the SIGPIPE handler API\n\nWorking di